when Kate Flannery exited the office for  the last time she did so having created  and embodied Meredith one of the  funniest secondary characters on  television but just what has Flannery  been up to since leaving Meredith Palmer  behind after nine long seasons the  office left the air on a high note with  the iconic wedding of two main  characters Dwight and Angela a send-off  that sat well with Flannery speaking to  the blog how to be a redhead she  explained I am so proud of the ending of  the office I felt that everything was  wrapped up so nicely it's added funny  and thoughtful and everything you want  in the finale I am so sad but I am so  proud it's a great feeling to be part of  such a respected and honored project the  end of the show also made Flannery feel  nostalgic and reflective which she  discussed in an essay she wrote for  Huffington Post  she wrote to be part of an ensemble on  TV as a gift I stopped counting lines I  was disappointed at first when my lines  would get cut but it dawned on me I  don't need to be the meat I don't need  to be the side dish I can be the onions  it's good to be the onions I fall in  love with make it when it came to  summing up the offices appeal to fans  and audiences around the world  Flannery put it just about as succinctly  as you can she wrote  Abraham Lincoln said most people are as  happy as they make up their minds to be  this show made its mind up to have heart  and soul and treat the audience like it  had a brain nowadays Flannery gets to  flex her musical muscles and her comedy  lounge act the lampshades in which she's  joined by fellow actor Scott Robinson  Flannery describes the act as a  male-female duo fresh from the cruise  ship circuit spinning pop and rock into  comedy gold as they work out the kinks  in their amusingly tortured relationship  the dual plays regularly mostly in  Southern California comedy clubs and for  a number of years they had a standing  gig at the IO Theatre in Hollywood  Flannery says it's been musically  interesting  we will gig out and host stand-up nights  and we've done a lot of charity events  and some private parties it's very  portable show so it's been really really  great for us  we've gotten around a lot doing it and  we've met a lot of people because of it  in addition to the lampshades flattery  also sings and performs with Glee star  Jane Lynch and Lynch's comedy cabaret  show see Jane sing the pair's working  relationship goes back to the early days  of a stage show called the real live  Brady Bunch  when Flannery served as Lynch's  understudy and acted in several of the  plays non Brady roles and while much of  see Jane sing seems to be improvised  Lynch says this simply isn't the case I  like to script every damn moment I build  a cage but then I bounce around freely  within the cage  Flannery herself however does seem to  keep things fresh it's always 360  nothing's the same twice for her so and  that keeps me alive and going what is  she gonna do now a film variety called a  thoroughly ingratiating touchingly  heartfelt comedy fourth man out tells  the story of Adam a small-town car  mechanic who after a night of drinking  comes out to his three lifelong friends  who are surprised to learn he is gay the  bulk of the film finds them attempting  to maintain the equilibrium in their  friendship while helping Adam find a  relationship of his own Flannery plays  Adams mother Karen and says the film is  a byproduct of an increasingly tolerant  audience and society in an interview  with the film's cast  she told Hollywood Chicago the world has  changed so much and younger kids have so  much less judgement about everything  they don't care to draw lines between  people I think that is fantastic and  this movie is the evolution of coming  out in America this is an amazing story  that represents that change  Parker Young who played one of Adams  friends in the film agreed he said our  generation is more aware of what we  think about it as individuals and we're  not listening to negative backlash when  we don't agree with it Flannery  maintains a robust presence on Twitter  and Instagram tweeting and posting  photos of a number of things including  her exploits offstage her time spent  with friends and other celebrities and  her slate of current and upcoming  projects she is also fond of retweeting  fans posts and a seemingly endless  stream of memes both of the office in  general and of her character Meredith  specifically  she doesn't always feel comfortable in  the virtual realm though in an interview  with Google  Flannery noted that engaging with fans  online can often be pretty difficult I  have to be a little more self conscious  than I normally would be and I just have  to sort of figure out like okay what  what am I really gonna who-who needs to  know what in fact she sees a problem  with social media personalities in  general I just feel like sometimes  there's such an egocentric thing that  happens with the sense of celebrity even  at the smallest level in the years since  the office closed for good Flannery has  filled her on-screen time with a range  of different projects most of them  independently produced films and  television shows she plays the role of  nosy next-door neighbor mrs. Jenkins and  stuck a 20-17 movie in which the main  character Darby is sentenced to a month  of house arrest in the same house as her  ex-boyfriend and his new fiancee  Flannery also took a part in fishbowl  California a film about a drunk  chronically ill Widow who takes in an  aimless 20-something finally Flannery  plays principal saperstein in the hulu  comedy series all night which deadline  describes as centering on an overnight  lock-in graduation party in which a  group of new grads will do whatever it  takes to make their remaining high  school dreams come true while none of  these projects have quite constituted an  office sized hit each has benefited  hugely from Flannery's wit and comedic  chops and considering the current pace  at which she's working it's safe to  assume that more shows and movies will  be added to the list in due course check  out one of our newest videos right here  plus even more looper videos about your  favorite shows are coming soon subscribe  to our YouTube channel and hit the bell  so you don't miss a single one  you  [Music]
 

